I recorded check 4 (can the slots hold a dense page?): the slots can hold the page, so the number of slots is not what limits the model. Check 3 (do text slots keep what image slots lose?) is stalled for one wake: the first job of its chain failed on a bug in its own check. I fixed the bug, but the 4-submissions-per-wake cap is spent, so the relaunch waits for the next wake.

## Check 4 — decided
I trained the stage-2 model on 100 dense pages only, then had it rewrite each page from its slots alone.

| pages | word recall before training ↑ | word recall after ↑ | after − before (95% CI) | pages better / worse |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| the 100 trained pages | .702 | **.921** | +21.9 pt [+18.5, +25.3] | 98 / 2, p 8e-27 |
| 100 held-out pages | .670 | .667 | −0.3 pt [−4.2, +3.6] | 32 / 66 |

- Word recall means the share of the page's words that come back.
- About 120 slots per page, 8 image tokens per slot, roughly 4 words per slot.
- The bar was 90%, so the slots have room. The flat held-out pages show this is memorisation, not a general gain.
- Training loss was still falling at the last step, so .921 is a minimum. This is one training on one seed.
- What it means for the stage-2 rebuild: change what training teaches (objective, data, steps), not the number of slots.
- The second training (fp32 master weights) was not run. The plan fixed beforehand ran it only if recall stayed under 90%.
- The missing health number (peak GPU memory of the 20-step test training) was in SLURM's accounting all along: 52 GB of 80.

## Check 3 — what happened this wake
- All 1,268 pages of the 500 questions are transcribed, with 0 empty.
- The 30-question test build wrote correct sets, but exited with code 4 on its own health check. That check was wrong in two ways:
  - it counted the slots inside a text chunk's length (256 text tokens + 33 slots = 289);
  - it counted image chunks as text chunks.
- I fixed the check in `scripts/slotcheck/build_text_sets.py`. Replayed on the test build's audit file, the new rule passes all 30 questions and catches both faults I planted. The fixed script itself has not run yet.
- The 3 jobs chained behind the test build could never start, so I cancelled them.
- In the test data, the answer text appears in the page transcription for 26 of 30 questions.

## Next wake
- The 30-question eval and the full set build run side by side.
- Then the judged eval on 500 questions, with image slots, text slots, and both.

## Budget
- 23 of 32 jobs used.
- About 15 of 30 GPU-hours used.

Nothing needed from you.
